d\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}{(0.54)}^{x+3}-2e & \\ge e \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}{(0.54)}^{x+3} & \\ge 3e \\\\ {(0.54)}^{x+3} & \\ge 4e.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, taking the natural logarithm of both sides and applying the laws of logarithms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡[(0.54)^{x+3}] & \\ge \\operatorname{ln}⁡(4e) \\\\ (x+3)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.54) & \\ge \\operatorname{ln}⁡(4e)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, note that $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.54)$ is a negative quantity, so when we divide both sides by it, we need to flip the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+3 & \\le \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4e)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.54)} \\\\ x & \\le \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4e)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.54)}-3\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/state.json" "file_sha256" "42c5ec637e5c38e12c083ae2e0aff7169f12acf2a2b83d141410aefb43ad3295"} {"question" "q-365308" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "89563438f069c3d0799b97e55e1becd211614e03a08255bf9c12aa841769557a"} {"question" "q-365308" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/state.json" "file_sha256" "42c5ec637e5c38e12c083ae2e0aff7169f12acf2a2b83d141410aefb43ad3295"} {"question" "q-365308" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x\\ge \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.54)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4e)}+3"] ["math" "x\\ge \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4e)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.54)}-3"] ["math" "x\\le \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.54)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2e)}+1"] ["math" "x\\le \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2e)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.54