lity ${e}^{x+1}<-2$ has no solutions." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/state.json" "file_sha256" "42c5ec637e5c38e12c083ae2e0aff7169f12acf2a2b83d141410aefb43ad3295"} {"question" "q-87872" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "89563438f069c3d0799b97e55e1becd211614e03a08255bf9c12aa841769557a"} {"question" "q-87872" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/state.json" "file_sha256" "42c5ec637e5c38e12c083ae2e0aff7169f12acf2a2b83d141410aefb43ad3295"} {"question" "q-87872" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x<-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "x<\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "x>\\frac{1}{4}"] ["text" "all real numbers"] ["text" "no solutions"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/state.json" "file_sha256" "42c5ec637e5c38e12c083ae2e0aff7169f12acf2a2b83d141410aefb43ad3295"} {"question" "q-87872" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "no solutions"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/state.json" "file_sha256" "42c5ec637e5c38e12c083ae2e0aff7169f12acf2a2b83d141410aefb43ad3295"} {"question" "q-87893" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $\\frac{3}{5}\\cdot {3}^{1-5x}+6>0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/state.json" "file_sha256" "42c5ec637e5c38e12c083ae2e0aff7169f12acf2a2b83d141410aefb43ad3295"} {"question" "q-87893" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Isolating the exponential term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5}\\cdot {3}^{1-5x}+6 & >0 \\\\ \\frac{3}{5}\\cdot {3}^{1-5x} & >-6 \\\\ {3}^{1-5x} & >-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause a power of a positive number is always greater than $0,$ we must have\n\n$$\n{3}^{1-5x}>0\n$$\n\nfor all values of $x.$\n\nTherefore, the inequality ${3}^{1-5x}>-10$ is satisfied for all real values of $x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/state.json" "file_sha256" "42c5ec637e5c38e12c083ae2e0aff7169f12acf2a2b83d141410aefb43ad3295"} {"question" "q-87893" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "89563438f069c3d0799b97e55e1becd211614e03a08255bf9c12aa841769557a"} {"question" "q-87893" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/state.json" "file_sha256" "42c5ec637e5c38e12c083ae2e0aff7169f12acf2a2b83d141410aefb43ad3295"} {"question" "q-87893" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x<3-{log}_{3}⁡(6)"] ["math" "x<5-{log}_{6}⁡(2)"] ["math" "x>6-{log}_{5}⁡(3)"] ["text" "all real numbers"] ["text" "no solutions"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/state.json" "file_sha256" "42c5ec637e5c38e12c083ae2e0aff7169f12acf2a2b83d141410aefb43ad3295"} {"question" "q-87893" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "all real numbers"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/state.json" "file_sha256" "42c5ec637e5c38e12c083ae2e0aff7169f12acf2a2b83d141410aefb43ad3295"} {"question" "q-115231" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $\\frac{3}{2}(0.43)^{4x+5}+4>-2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/state.json" "file_sha256" "42c5ec637e5c38e12c083ae2e0aff7169f12acf2a2b83d141410aefb43ad3295"} {"question" "q-115231" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Isolating the exponential term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}(0.43)^{4x+5}+4 & >-2 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}(0.43)^{4x+5} & >-6 \\\\ (0.43)^{4x+5} & >-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause a power of a positive number is always greater than $0,$ we must have\n\n$$\n(0.43)^{4x+5}>0\n$$\n\nfor all values of $x.$\n\nTherefore, the inequality $(0.43)^{4x+5}>-4$ is satisfied for all real values of $x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/state.json" "file_sha256" "42c5ec637e5c38e12c083ae2e0aff7169f12acf2a2b83d141410aefb43ad3295"} {"question" "q-115231" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "89563438f069c3d0799b97e55e1becd211614e03a08255bf9c12aa841769557a"} {"question" "q-115231" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/state.json" "file_sha256" "42c5ec637e5c38e12c083ae2e0aff7169f12acf2a2b83d141410aefb43ad3295"} {"question" "q-115231" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x>-4"] ["math" "x>0"] ["math" "x>2"] ["text" "all real numbers"] ["text" "no solutions"]] "cate