eld.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/state.json" "file_sha256" "42c5ec637e5c38e12c083ae2e0aff7169f12acf2a2b83d141410aefb43ad3295"} {"question" "q-87874" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x<\\frac{1}{5}"] ["math" "x<\\frac{4}{5}"] ["math" "x>\\frac{1}{5}"] ["text" "all real numbers"] ["text" "no solutions"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/state.json" "file_sha256" "42c5ec637e5c38e12c083ae2e0aff7169f12acf2a2b83d141410aefb43ad3295"} {"question" "q-87874" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "no solutions"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/state.json" "file_sha256" "42c5ec637e5c38e12c083ae2e0aff7169f12acf2a2b83d141410aefb43ad3295"} {"question" "q-87908" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $5\\cdot {2}^{x}<{3}^{2-x}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/state.json" "file_sha256" "42c5ec637e5c38e12c083ae2e0aff7169f12acf2a2b83d141410aefb43ad3295"} {"question" "q-87908" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Taking the natural logarithm of both sides and applying the laws of logarithms, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5\\cdot {2}^{x} & <{3}^{2-x} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(5\\cdot {2}^{x}) & <\\operatorname{ln}⁡({3}^{2-x}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡5+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({2}^{x}) & <\\operatorname{ln}⁡({3}^{2-x}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡5+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 & <(2-x)\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡5+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 & <2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\ x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 & <2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 \\\\ x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) & <2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 \\\\ x & <\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/state.json" "file_sha256" "42c5ec637e5c38e12c083ae2e0aff7169f12acf2a2b83d141410aefb43ad3295"} {"question" "q-87908" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "89563438f069c3d0799b97e55e1becd211614e03a08255bf9c12aa841769557a"} {"question" "q-87908" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/state.json" "file_sha256" "42c5ec637e5c38e12c083ae2e0aff7169f12acf2a2b83d141410aefb43ad3295"} {"question" "q-87908" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x<\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}"] ["math" "x<\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}"] ["math" "x<\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}"] ["math" "x>\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}"] ["math" "x>\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/state.json" "file_sha256" "42c5ec637e5c38e12c083ae2e0aff7169f12acf2a2b83d141410aefb43ad3295"} {"question" "q-87908" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x<\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/state.json" "file_sha256" "42c5ec637e5c38e12c083ae2e0aff7169f12acf2a2b83d141410aefb43ad3295"} {"question" "q-115250" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality ${5}^{x-1}<{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2-x}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/state.json" "file_sha256" "42c5ec637e5c38e12c083ae2e0aff7169f12acf2a2b83d141410aefb43ad3295"} {"question" "q-115250" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Taking the natural logarithm of both sides and applying the laws of logarithms, we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{5}^{x-1} & <{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2-x} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({5}^{x-1}) & <\\operatorname{ln}⁡[{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2-x}] \\\\ (x-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 & <(2-x)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\ (x-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 & <(2-x)(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\ (x-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 & <(2-x)(0-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\ (x-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 & <(x-2)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 & <x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 & <\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) & <\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ x & <\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/state.json" "file_sha256" "42c5ec637e5c38e12c083ae2e0aff7169f12acf2a2b83d141410aefb43ad3295"} {"question" "q-115250" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "89563438f069c3d0799b97e55e1becd211614e03a08255bf9c12aa841769557a"} {"question" "q-115250" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/state.json" "file_sha256" "42c5ec637e5c38e12c083ae2e0aff7169f12acf2a2b83d141410aefb43ad3295"} {"question" "q-115250" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x<2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-3"] ["math" "x<5\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+3"] ["math" "x<\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}"] ["math" "x>2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-3"] ["math" "x>\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/state.json" "file_sha256" "42c5ec637e5c38e12c083ae2e0aff7169f12acf2a2b83d141410aefb43ad3295"} {"question" "q-115250" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x<\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/state.json" "file_sha256" "42c5ec637e5c38e12c083ae2e0aff7169f12acf2a2b83d141410aefb43ad3295"} {"question" "q-365326" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $3{(\\frac{1}{5})}^{x-2}>{3}^{2-3x}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/state.json" "file_sha256" "42c5ec637e5c38e12c083ae2e0aff7169f12acf2a2b83d141410aefb43ad3295"} {"question" "q-365326" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Taking the natural logarithm of both sides and applying the laws of logarithms, we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{(\\frac{1}{5})}^{x-2} & >{3}^{2-3x} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡[3{(\\frac{1}{5})}^{x-2}] & >\\operatorname{ln}⁡({3}^{2-3x}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡3+\\operatorname{ln}⁡[{(\\frac{1}{5})}^{x-2}] & >\\operatorname{ln}⁡({3}^{2-3x}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡3+(x-2)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{5}) & >(2-3x)\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡3+(x-2)(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5) & >(2-3x)\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡3+(x-2)(0-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5) & >(2-3x)\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡3+(2-x)\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 & >(2-3x)\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡3+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 & >2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-3x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\ 3x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 & >2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 \\\\ x(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5) & >\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 \\\\ x & >\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/state.json" "file_sha256" "42c5ec637e5c38e12c083ae2e0aff7169f12acf2a2b83d141410aefb43ad3295"} {"question" "q-365326" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "89563438f069c3d0799b97e55e1becd211614e03a08255bf9c12aa841769557a"} {"question" "q-365326" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/state.json" "file_sha256" "42c5ec637e5c38e12c083ae2e0aff7169f12acf2a2b83d141410aefb43ad3295"} {"question" "q-365326" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x<\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}"] ["math" "x<\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}"] ["math" "x>\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}"] ["math" "x>\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}"] ["math" "x>\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/state.json" "file_sha256" "42c5ec637e5c38e12c083ae2e0aff7169f12acf2a2b83d141410aefb43ad3295"} {"question" "q-365326" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x>\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/state.json" "file_sha256" "42c5ec637e5c38e12c083ae2e0aff7169f12acf2a2b83d141410aefb43ad3295"} {"question" "q-365323" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality ${4}^{1-2x}\\le 3\\cdot {5}^{2-3x}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/state.json" "file_sha256" "42c5ec637e5c38e12c083ae2e0aff7169f12acf2a2b83d141410aefb43ad3295"} {"question" "q-365323" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Taking the natural logarithm of both sides and applying the laws of logarithms, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{4}^{1-2x} & \\le 3\\cdot {5}^{2-3x} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({4}^{1-2x}) & \\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡(3\\cdot {5}^{2-3x}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({4}^{1-2x}) & \\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({5}^{2-3x}) \\\\ (1-2x)\\operatorname{ln}⁡4 & \\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡3+(2-3x)\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡4-2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4 & \\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡3+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-3x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 \\\\ 3x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4 & \\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡3+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4 \\\\ x(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4) & \\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡3+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4 \\\\ x & \\le \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/state.json" "file_sha256" "42c5ec637e5c38e12c083ae2e0aff7169f12acf2a2b83d141410aefb43ad3295"} {"question" "q-365323" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "89563438f069c3d0799b97e55e1becd211614e03a08255bf9c12aa841769557a"} {"question" "q-365323" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/state.json" "file_sha256" "42c5ec637e5c38e12c083ae2e0aff7169f12acf2a2b83d141410aefb43ad3295"} {"question" "q-365323" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x\\ge \\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡5+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}"] ["math" "x\\ge \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}"] ["math" "x\\le \\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5+\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}"] ["math" "x\\le \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}"] ["math" "x\\le \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/state.json" "file_sha256" "42c5ec637e5c38e12c083ae2e0aff7169f12acf2a2b83d141410aefb43ad3295"} {"question" "q-365323" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x\\le \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/state.json" "file_sha256" "42c5ec637e5c38e12c083ae2e0aff7169f12acf2a2b83d141410aefb43ad3295"} {"question" "q-115248" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality ${7}^{x+1}>{5}^{x-1}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/state.json" "file_sha256" "42c5ec637e5c38e12c083ae2e0aff7169f12acf2a2b83d141410aefb43ad3295"} {"question" "q-115248" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Taking the natural logarithm of both sides and applying the laws of logarithms, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{7}^{x+1} & >{5}^{x-1} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({7}^{x+1}) & >\\operatorname{ln}⁡({5}^{x-1}) \\\\ (x+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡7 & >(x-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 \\\\ x\\operatorname{ln}⁡7+\\operatorname{ln}⁡7 & >x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 \\\\ x\\operatorname{ln}⁡7-x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 & >-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡7 \\\\ x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡7-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5) & >-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡7 \\\\ x & >-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5+\\operatorname{ln}⁡7}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡7-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5} \\\\ x & >\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5+\\operatorname{ln}⁡7}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡7}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/state.json" "file_sha256" "42c5ec637e5c38e12c083ae2e0aff7169f12acf2a2b83d141410aefb43ad3295"} {"question" "q-115248" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "89563438f069c3d0799b97e55e1becd211614e03a08255bf9c12aa841769557a"} {"question" "q-115248" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/state.json" "file_sha256" "42c5ec637e5c38e12c083ae2e0aff7169f12acf2a2b83d141410aefb43ad3295"} {"question" "q-115248" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x>-\\frac{7}{5}"] ["math" "x>\\frac{5}{7}"] ["math" "x>\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5+\\operatorname{ln}⁡7}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡7}"] ["math" "x>\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡7}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡7+\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}"] ["math" "x>\\operatorname{ln}⁡7-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/state.json" "file_sha256" "42c5ec637e5c38e12c083ae2e0aff7169f12acf2a2b83d141410aefb43ad3295"} {"question" "q-115248" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x>\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5+\\operatorname{ln}⁡7}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡7}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/state.json" "file_sha256" "42c5ec637e5c38e12c083ae2e0aff7169f12acf2a2b83d141410aefb43ad3295"} {"question" "e-7657" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $4e^x - 5 >  0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/example-7657.json" "file_sha256" "69bd112804b1d41c9445f39fb981c3c57ed53766198ce14104690b0276cb8157"} {"question" "e-7657" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Isolating the exponential term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{e}^{x}-5 & >0 \\\\ 4{e}^{x} & >5 \\\\ {e}^{x} & >\\frac{5}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, taking the natural logarithm of both sides and applying the laws of logarithms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{x}) & >\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{5}{4}) \\\\ x & >\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/example-7657.json" "file_sha256" "69bd112804b1d41c9445f39fb981c3c57ed53766198ce14104690b0276cb8157"} {"question" "e-7703" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $5 \\cdot \\left( \\dfrac{3}{4} \\right)^x + 2 \\geq 12.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/example-7703.json" "file_sha256" "ee1aa86a0193034aa0e0591b57e616a406f9cd699ad2ba8464a29af281d2b0a8"} {"question" "e-7703" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Isolating the exponential term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5\\cdot {(\\frac{3}{4})}^{x}+2 & \\ge 12 \\\\ 5\\cdot {(\\frac{3}{4})}^{x} & \\ge 10 \\\\ {(\\frac{3}{4})}^{x} & \\ge 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, taking the natural logarithm of both sides and applying the laws of logarithms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡[{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{x}] & \\ge \\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{4}) & \\ge \\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4) & \\ge \\operatorname{ln}⁡2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, note that $\\ln 3 - \\ln 4$ is a negative quantity, so when we divide both sides by it, we need to flip the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & \\le \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/example-7703.json" "file_sha256" "ee1aa86a0193034aa0e0591b57e616a406f9cd699ad2ba8464a29af281d2b0a8"} {"question" "e-7704" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $4 \\cdot 3^{8-x} + 12 > 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/example-7704.json" "file_sha256" "46d638f88649a84d3dc51a88756dba8dd8144586f86c338fbe788db11df9b265"} {"question" "e-7704" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Isolating the exponential term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\cdot {3}^{8-x}+12 & >0 \\\\ 4\\cdot {3}^{8-x} & >-12 \\\\ {3}^{8-x} & >-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause a power of a positive number is always greater than $0,$ we must have\n\n$$\n3^{8-x} > 0\n$$\n\nfor all values of $x.$\n\nTherefore, the inequality $3^{8-x} > -3$ is satisfied for all real values of $x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/example-7704.json" "file_sha256" "46d638f88649a84d3dc51a88756dba8dd8144586f86c338fbe788db11df9b265"} {"question" "e-7660" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $3 \\cdot 5^x <   7^{3-x}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/example-7660.json" "file_sha256" "73086c8c1bdb06e0263dd1475ac0acb9acbfdd24ce0d07d1af32747a7e47d700"} {"question" "e-7660" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Taking the natural logarithm of both sides and applying the laws of logarithms, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\cdot {5}^{x} & <{7}^{3-x} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(3\\cdot {5}^{x}) & <\\operatorname{ln}⁡({7}^{3-x}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡3+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({5}^{x}) & <\\operatorname{ln}⁡({7}^{3-x}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡3+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 & <(3-x)\\operatorname{ln}⁡7 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡3+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 & <3\\operatorname{ln}⁡7-x\\operatorname{ln}⁡7 \\\\ x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡7 & <3\\operatorname{ln}⁡7-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\ x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡5+\\operatorname{ln}⁡7) & <3\\operatorname{ln}⁡7-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\ x & <\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡7-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5+\\operatorname{ln}⁡7}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/example-7660.json" "file_sha256" "73086c8c1bdb06e0263dd1475ac0acb9acbfdd24ce0d07d1af32747a7e47d700"}] "usage" {"e-7704" [] "e-7703" [] "e-7660" [] "e-7657" []} "basis" 893 "retractions" [[17592186157068 :question/problem "Solve the inequality $4e^x - 5 > 0$."] [17592186157068 :question/worked-solution "Isolating the exponential term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}4e^{x} - 5 & > 0 \\\\ 4e^{x} & > 5 \\\\ e^{x} & > \\frac{5}{4}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThen, taking the natural logarithm of both sides and applying the laws of logarithms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\ln (e^{x}) & > \\ln (\\frac{5}{4}) \\\\ x & > \\ln 5 - \\ln 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"] [17592186157075 :question/problem "Solve the inequality $5 \\cdot \\left(\\dfrac{3}{4} \\right)^x + 2 \\geq 12$."] [17592186157075 :question/worked-solution "Isolating the exponential term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\cdot (\\frac{3}{4})^{x} + 2 & \\ge 12 \\\\ 5 \\cdot (\\frac{3}{4})^{x} & \\ge 10 \\\\ (\\frac{3}{4})^{x} & \\ge 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThen, taking the natural logarithm of both sides and applying the laws of logarithms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\ln [(\\frac{3}{4})^{x}] & \\ge \\ln 2 \\\\ x\\ln (\\frac{3}{4}) & \\ge \\ln 2 \\\\ x(\\ln 3 - \\ln 4) & \\ge \\ln 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nLastly, note that $\\ln 3 - \\ln 4$ is a negative quantity, so when we divide both sides by it, we need to flip the inequality:\n\n$$\nx \\mid \\le \\frac{\\ln 2}{\\ln 3 - \\ln 4}\n$$"] [17592186157076 :question/problem "Solve the inequality $4 \\cdot 3^{8-x} + 12 > 0$."] [17592186157076 :question/worked-solution "Isolating the exponential term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\cdot 3^{8 - x} + 12 & > 0 \\\\ 4 \\cdot 3^{8 - x} & > - 12 \\\\ 3^{8 - x} & > - 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBecause a power of a positive number is always greater than $0$, we must have\n\n$$\n3^{8-x} > 0\n$$\n\nfor all values of $x$.\n\nTherefore, the inequality $3^{8-x} > -3$ is satisfied for all real values of $x$."] [17592186157069 :question/problem "Solve the inequality $3 \\cdot 5^x < 7^{3-x}$."] [17592186157069 :question/worked-solution "Taking the natural logarithm of both sides and applying the laws of logarithms, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\cdot 5^{x} & < 7^{3 - x} \\\\ \\ln (3 \\cdot 5^{x}) & < \\ln (7^{3 - x}) \\\\ \\ln 3 + \\ln (5^{x}) & < \\ln (7^{3 - x}) \\\\ \\ln 3 + x\\ln 5 & < (3 - x)\\ln 7 \\\\ \\ln 3 + x\\ln 5 & < 3\\ln 7 - x\\ln 7 \\\\ x\\ln 5 + x\\ln 7 & < 3\\ln 7 - \\ln 3 \\\\ x(\\ln 5 + \\ln 7) & < 3\\ln 7 - \\ln 3 \\\\ x & < \\frac{3\\ln 7 - \\ln 3}{\\ln 5 + \\ln 7}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
